{"duration_api_ms":152432,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0204548c-a824-57b7-bea3-1783011bc81a","total_cost_usd":1.0650126,"usage":{"input_tokens":66,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38218,"cache_read_input_tokens":2214223,"output_tokens":15808,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2395},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38218,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1248,"cache_read_input_tokens":83903,"cache_creation_input_tokens":540,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":540},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":66,"outputTokens":15808,"cacheReadInputTokens":2214223,"cacheCreationInputTokens":38218,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0650126,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2395,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":38218,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":34,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've ported the shapeFragment cache into the sdkjs source, built it, regenerated the V8 snapshot and re-measured. It cuts x2t CPU time by 14–24 % on large xlsx → pdf, and every page of the output is pixel-identical (2 605 of 2 605). All three acceptance commands pass, `theseus validate` reports no errors, and the work is committed as `a006004`.\n\n**What I did**\n- **Source patch:** the change is in `cell/view/StringRender.js` (sdkjs `9cea536`, +34/−1). It is saved as `.theseus/diagnosis/PKT-0077-sdkjs-shape-cache.patch` and can be applied to sdkjs with `git apply`. It uses the same cache key and replay logic as the PKT-0069 prototype. The original function body is renamed `private_shapeFragment`, and recording happens in `private_HandleItem`.\n- **Build:** I built the cell bundle with webpack twice from the same checkout, once clean and once patched. That way the only difference between the two sides is the patch; the installed 9.3.7 file comes from a different build.\n- **Snapshot:** the new script `.theseus/oracle/perf/sdkjs-mirror.sh` creates a mirror install for each side and runs `x2t -create-js-snapshots` there, so each gets a fresh `sdk-all.bin`. The installed files were not changed; I checked their modification times.\n- **Measurement:** the new script `.theseus/oracle/perf/x2t-cpu-ab.py` alternates baseline and patched runs. Medians of 2 runs each:\n\n  | Sample | Baseline | Patched | Saving |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | 1 sheet, 25k rows | 17.8 s | 14.9 s | 16 % |\n  | 1 sheet, 50k rows, numbers only | 36.6 s | 31.5 s | 14 % |\n  | 1 sheet, 50k rows | 35.5 s | 26.8 s | 24 % |\n\n  PKT-0069's 26 % for the numbers-only file did not reproduce. Baseline runs vary by about ±2 s on this VM, so expect roughly 15–25 %.\n- **Results note:** written to the new `.theseus/diagnosis/PKT-0077-shape-cache-source.md`. I left `PKT-0069-shape-cache.md` alone because it is not in this packet's target files.\n\n**Risk, and the follow-up I requested**\nThe cache key doesn't record whether the font file has loaded yet. That doesn't matter in x2t, where all fonts are local and the process is short-lived. In the browser editor, though, fonts load lazily, so text shaped with a fallback font could keep being drawn with the fallback after the real font arrives. I recorded a request in `.theseus/spawn/` to clear the cache when fonts finish loading (or limit it to x2t) and to prepare the upstream PR. I did not open the PR myself, since that is a public action.\n\n**Not done**\n- I did not run the sdkjs unit tests (QUnit, which run in a browser) against the patched build. The page-by-page comparison was the only regression check.\n- I did not measure how often the cache hits.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas**\n- On this shared 7 GB VM the webpack build needs `NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=2500`. The previous attempt was killed for running out of memory without it.\n- For x2t performance comparisons: build both sides from one checkout, give each its own mirror and snapshot, and alternate the runs.\n- Any memo cache in sdkjs text shaping has to handle fonts loading lazily in the browser.\n\nThe executor log, the lessons section and the friction line are filled in.","ttft_ms":1481,"type":"result","duration_ms":698052,"uuid":"09787785-f9df-4ac2-9d25-810369238d7b","ttft_stream_ms":896,"time_to_request_ms":320,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":209,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":16,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":18,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":13,"query_setup":2,"auto_mode_context_wait":6,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":20,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":7},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":34,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":142,"time_to_request_major_faults":29,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":214,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":204,"process_anon_mib_result":142,"process_peak_rss_mib":255,"process_cpu_ms_turn":7172,"process_wall_ms_turn":698052,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1915,"process_wall_ms_streaming":121058,"main_stream_count":33,"ma